BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Celebrating Obon
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260815T000000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260815T235959
DTSTAMP:20260728T103734Z
UID:469399a20a298492fe195e3281139cb0@family-events-agent
SEQUENCE:0
CATEGORIES:children,play,toddler,museum,family
DESCRIPTION:Organizer: Pretend City Children's Museum - Events\\nAges: 0-6
 0 months\\nCategory: Music & Dance\\n\\nJoin us as we celebrate Obon\, a m
 eaningful Japanese tradition that honors and remembers ancestors through d
 ance\, storytelling\, and community. Families are invited to learn about t
 hemes of remembrance\, gratitude\, and connection! \nTimes: 11am &amp\; 2
 :30pm\nActivities and times subject to change. \nAbout the play partner:
  Orange County Buddhist Church (OCBC) \nThe Orange County Buddhist Churc
 h (OCBC) is a Jōdo Shinshū (Shin Buddhist) temple located in Anahei
 m\, California\, and a member of the Buddhist Churches of America&#8217\;s
  (BCA) Southern District. Originally established to serve the Japanese A
 merican community\, OCBC has grown into a vibrant center of Shin Buddhist 
 life in Southern California. The church achieved independent status in 196
 5 and has been serving the greater Orange County region for over six decad
 es. \nOCBC is affiliated with the Jōdo Shinshū Hongwanji-ha traditio
 n\, whose head temple (Nishi Honganji) is located in Kyoto\, Japan.\\n\
 \nMore info: https://www.pretendcity.org/events/celebrating-obon/
LOCATION:Pretend City Children's Museum - Events\, 29 Hubble\, Irvine\, CA
 \, 92618
URL:https://www.pretendcity.org/events/celebrating-obon/
