DESCRIPTION:Organizer: Pretend City Children's Museum - Events\\nAges: 0-6
 0 months\\nCategory: Play & Games\\n\\nGet ready for a wild adventure! Fam
 ilies will journey through the desert and forest on a pretend hike filled 
 with live animals\, nature discoveries\, and hands-on exploration. \nTime
 s: 11am &amp\; 2:30pm  \n*Please note programming lasts 10-30 minutes.
  \nIncluded in museum admission. Space is limited! Book your tickets no
 w. \n*Members do not require a reservation. \n*Events and dates are subj
 ect to change. \nAbout the play partner: \nEnvironmental Nature Center
 ’s mission is to provide transformative experiences through connection w
 ith nature. \nFrequently Asked Questions \nIs this program included wit
 h museum admission?\nYes. Habitat Hike Animal Encounter is included with 
 regular museum admission. \nWhat animals will families meet?\nFamilies ma
 y meet 3–4 live animals from desert and forest habitats. Animals may v
 ary by program. \nWhat are biofacts?\nBiofacts are natural items that com
 e from animals\, such as feathers\, fur\, bones\, or shells\, that help ch
 ildren learn more about wildlife. \nHow long does the program last?\nEach
  presentation lasts approximately 10–30 minutes.\\n\\nMore info: https
 ://www.pretendcity.org/events/habitat-hike-animal-encounter-with-environme
 ntal-nature-center/
